WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.740
God, isn't this picture so fake?

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.280
This is AI, and it makes me sad because it is enjoyable.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:11.740
Really visually, I think that the spray back there, the figures in the back, of course the Pink Panther,

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:19.920
it all comes together so this brightness of the pink pops against all the sort of muted colors, but it's not real.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:25.000
Either is this one, and then you can look, there's the account where I double-checked that it's AI.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:34.640
My question is, given how many great images there are out of the protests, why would somebody put these out there?

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.580
I think it's for a few reasons, profit.

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:44.700
And it feels appealing for a lot of international people of a certain age, the age that really loves AI.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:51.580
The Pink Panther does speak to their memories of what they think of as being related to France.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:56.900
I think for people like me, I didn't really grow up with the Pink Panther except for in commercials.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.860
It's visually surprising, again, because of the pink against the darkness.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:01.880
And it's funny.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:07.660
And I do think weaponized frivolity is an important part of protest.

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:17.880
That's when we make funny things to basically make fun of people like the police who is attacking people who are from their same country.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:30.040
But when that term came up, it was in a time where you didn't have AI, where you didn't have people profiting off of something that diminishes a movement.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:36.180
Weaponized frivolity originally comes out of 20th century movements that were largely ephemeral.

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:52.060
By making this something that gets shared around the world, you diminish the real things that are happening, but also the future of protesting and using your voice in a nation that claims to have free speech.
